  "pageSize": 50,
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6a0",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2819,
      "bookHadithIndex": 201,
      "text": "It was narrated from As-Sab bin Jaththamah that:he gave the Messenger of Allah an onager when he was in Al-Abwa or in Waddan, but the Messenger of Allah gave it back to him. \"And when the Messenger of Allah saw the expression on my face he said: \"We only gave it back to you because we are in Ihram",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2819-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2819-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2819-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6a1",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2820,
      "bookHadithIndex": 202,
      "text": "It was narrated from As-Sab bin Jaththamah that:the Prophet came, and when he was in Waddan, he saw an onager, but he gave it back to him and said: \"'We are in Ihram, we cannot eat game",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2820-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2820-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2820-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6a2",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2821,
      "bookHadithIndex": 203,
      "text": "It was narrated from 'Ata' that Ibn 'Abbas said to Zaid bin Arqam:\"Do you not know that the Prophet was given a piece of game meant when he was in Ihram and he did not accept it?\" He said: \"Yes",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2821-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2821-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2821-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6a3",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2821,
      "bookHadithIndex": 204,
      "text": "It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:\"Zaid bin Arqam came and Ibn Abbas said to him, reminding him: \"What did you tell me about the game meat that was given to the Messenger of Allah when he was in Ihram?\" He said: \"Yes, a man gave him a piece of game meat but he returned it and said: 'We cannot eat it, we are in Ihram",
      "grades": []
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6a4",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2822,
      "bookHadithIndex": 205,
      "text": "It was narrated that Ibn Abbas said:\"As-Sab bin Jaththamah gave the Messenger of Allah the leg of an onager that was dripping with blood when he was in Ihram, at Qudaid, and he returned it to him",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2822-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2822-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2822-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6a5",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2823,
      "bookHadithIndex": 206,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn Abbas:That As-Sab bin Jaththamah gave the Prophet some onager (meat) when he was in Ihram and he returned it to him",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2823-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2823-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2823-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6a6",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2824,
      "bookHadithIndex": 207,
      "text": "It was narrated that Abdullah bin Abi Qatadah said:\"My father set out with the Messenger of Allah in the year of Al-Hudaybiyah, and his companions entered Ihram, but he did not. (He said:) 'While I was with my companions, some of them laughed at others. I looked and saw an onager. I stabbed it then asked them to help, but they refused to help me. We ate from its meat, and we were afraid that we would be intercepted (by the enemy) so I followed the Messenger of Allah, sometimes making my horse gallop and sometimes traveling at a regular place. I met a man from Ghifar at midnight and said: Where did you leave the Messenger of Allah? He said: I left him when he was napping in As-Suqya. I caught up with him and said: O messenger of Allah! Your Companions convey their greetings of Salam to you, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. They were afraid that they may be intercepted and cut off from you, so wait for them. Then I said: O Messenger of Allah, I caught an onager and I have some of it. He said to the People: Eat, and they were I Ihram",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2824-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2824-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2824-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6a7",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2825,
      "bookHadithIndex": 208,
      "text": "It was narrated that Yahya bin Abi Kathir said:\"Abdullah bin Abu Qatadah said that his father told him, that he went out with the Messenger of Allah on the campaign of Al-Hudaybiyah. He said: 'They entered Ihram for 'Umrah apart from me. I hunted an onager and fed my companions with it, when they were in Ihram. Then, I went to the Messenger of Allah and told him that we had some of it meat left over. HE said: Eat, and they were in Ihram",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2825-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2825-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2825-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6a8",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2826,
      "bookHadithIndex": 209,
      "text": "Abdullah bin Abi Qatadah narrated from his father that:they were on a march, somr of them in Ihram and some not in Ihram. He said: \"I saw an onager so I mounted my horse and picked up a spear. I asked them to help me but they refused to help me. I snatched a whip from one of them and chased the onager and caught it. They ate of it but they were scared. The prophet was asked about that and he said: 'Did you pint (at it) or help him?' They said, 'No.' He said: Then eat",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2826-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2826-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2826-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6a9",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2827,
      "bookHadithIndex": 210,
      "text": "It was narrated that Jabir said:\"I heard that Messenger of Allah say: 'Land game is permissible for you so long as you do not hunt it, and it is not hunted for you.'\" (Daif) Abu Abdur Rahman (An-Nasai) said: 'Amar bin Abi Amr Is not strong in Hadith, even they Malik reported from him",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2827-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2827-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2827-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6aa",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2828,
      "bookHadithIndex": 211,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah said:\"There are five (animals) for which there is no sin on the Muhrim if he kills them: Crows, kites, scorpions, mice and vicious dogs",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2828-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2828-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2828-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6ab",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2829,
      "bookHadithIndex": 212,
      "text": "It was narrated from Aishah that the Prophet said:\"There are five which the Muhrim may kill: snakes, mice, kites, speckled crows and vicious dogs",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2829-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2829-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2829-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6ac",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2830,
      "bookHadithIndex": 213,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah gave permission fro the Muhrim to kill five kinds of animals:crows, kites, mice and vicious dogs",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2830-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2830-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2830-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6ad",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2831,
      "bookHadithIndex": 214,
      "text": "It was narrated from Saeed bin Al-Musayyab that:a woman enter upon Aishah, and in her hand was an iron-footed stick. She said: \"What is this?\" she (Aishah) Said: \"It is for these geckos, because the Prophet of Allah told us, that there was nothing that did not try to extinguish the fire for Ihram except for this animals, so he told us to kill it. And he forbade us to kill harmless snakes, except for the snake with two lines on its back, and the snake with a short tail, for the snatch away the eyesight and cause tat which is in women's wombs to be miscarried",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2831-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2831-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2831-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6ae",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2832,
      "bookHadithIndex": 215,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn Umar that:the Prophet said \"There are five kinds of animals for which there is no sin on the one who kills them when he is in a state of Ihram: Kites, mice, vicious dogs, scorpions and crows.\" (Sahih) Chpater 87. Killing Kites",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2832-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2832-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2832-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6af",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2833,
      "bookHadithIndex": 216,
      "text": "It was narrated that Ibn Umar said:\"A man said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what animals may we kill when we are in Ihram?' He said: \"there are five for which there is no sin in killing them: Kites, crows, mice, scorpions and vicious dogs",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2833-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2833-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2833-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6b0",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2834,
      "bookHadithIndex": 217,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn Umar that:the Prophet was asked what the Muhrim may kill. He said: \"He may kill scorpions the evil creature (mice), Kites, crows and vicious dogs",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2834-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2834-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2834-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6b1",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2835,
      "bookHadithIndex": 218,
      "text": "It was narrated from Salim that his father said:\"The Prophet said: 'There are five kinds of animals for which there is no sin on the one who kills them, whether he is in Ihram or not: Mice, kites, crows, scorpions and vicious dogs.'\" (Sahih) Chpater 89. What The Muhrim May Not Kill",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2835-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2835-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2835-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6b2",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2836,
      "bookHadithIndex": 219,
      "text": "It was narrated that Ibn Abi ammar said:\"I asked Jabir bin Abdulla about hyenas, and he told me to eat them. I said: \"Is it not game? He said: 'Yes' I said: 'Did you hear that from the Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Yes",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2836-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2836-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6b3",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2837,
      "bookHadithIndex": 220,
      "text": "It was narrated that Ibn Abbas said:\"The Prophet married Maimunah when he was in Ihram",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2837-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Shadh"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2837-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Shadh"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2837-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6b4",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2838,
      "bookHadithIndex": 221,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn Abbas:That the Messenger of Allah got married when in Ihram",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2838-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "-"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2838-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6b5",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2839,
      "bookHadithIndex": 222,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn Abbas:That the Messenger of Allah married Maimunah when they were both in Ihram",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2839-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Shadh"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2839-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Shadh"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2839-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6b6",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2840,
      "bookHadithIndex": 223,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn Abbas:That the Messenger of Allah married Maimunah when he was in Ihram",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2840-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Shadh"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2840-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Shadh"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2840-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6b7",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2841,
      "bookHadithIndex": 224,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn Abbas:That the Prophet married Maimunah when he was in Ihram",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2841-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Shadh"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2841-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Shadh"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2841-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6b8",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2842,
      "bookHadithIndex": 225,
      "text": "Uthman bin Affan said:\"The Messenger of Allah said: 'The Muhrim should not get married, or propose marriage, or arrange a marriage for some else",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2842-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2842-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2842-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6b9",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2843,
      "bookHadithIndex": 226,
      "text": "It was narrated from Aban bin Uthamn, from his father:That the Prophet forbade the Muhrim to get married, arrange a marriage for anyone else, or propose marriage",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2843-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2843-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2843-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6ba",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2844,
      "bookHadithIndex": 227,
      "text": "Uthaman bin Affan narrated that the Prohet said:\"The Muhrim should not get or propose marriage",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2844-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2844-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2844-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6bb",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2845,
      "bookHadithIndex": 228,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn Abbas:That the Messenger of Allah was treated by means of cupping when he was in Ihram",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2845-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2845-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2845-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6bc",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2846,
      "bookHadithIndex": 229,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn Abbas that:The Prophet was treated by means of cupping when he was Ihram",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2846-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2846-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2846-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6bd",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2847,
      "bookHadithIndex": 230,
      "text": "It was narrated that Ibn Abbas said:\"Prophet was treated by means of cupping when he was in Ihram.\" (Diaf) Chpater 93. Cupping To Treat The Muhrim For A Disease he Is Suffering From",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2847-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2847-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2847-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6be",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2848,
      "bookHadithIndex": 231,
      "text": "It was narrated from Jabir:That the Prophet was treated by means of cupping when he was in Ihram for a contusion that he had suffered. (Diaf)",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2848-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2848-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2848-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6bf",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2849,
      "bookHadithIndex": 232,
      "text": "It was narrated from Anas:That the Messenger of Allah was treated by means of cupping when he was in Ihram on the top of the foot for contusion that he had suffered. (Daif)",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2849-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2849-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2849-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6c0",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2850,
      "bookHadithIndex": 233,
      "text": "Abdullah bin Buhayanah narrated:That the Messenger of Allah was treated by means of cupping in the middle of his head, when he was in Ihram, in Lahi Jamal, on the road to Makkah",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2850-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2850-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2850-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6c1",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2851,
      "bookHadithIndex": 234,
      "text": "It was narrated from Kab bin Ujra:That he was with the Messenger of Allah in Ihram and he suffered an infestation of head lice. The Messenger of Allah commanded him to shave his head and told him: \"Fast for three days, or fed six poor persons two Mudds earch, or sacrifice a sheep. Whichever one of these you do will be sufficient for you",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2851-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2851-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2851-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6c2",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2852,
      "bookHadithIndex": 235,
      "text": "It was narrated that Kab bin Ujrah said:\"I entered Ihram, then I had a severe infestation of head lice. News of that reached Prophet, and he came to me when I was cooking something in a pot for my companions, he touched my head with his finger and said: 'Go and shave it, and give charity to six poor persions",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2852-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2852-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2852-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6c3",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2853,
      "bookHadithIndex": 236,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn Abbas:That a man was with the Messenger of Allah, and his she-camel broke his neck when he was in Ihra, and he died. The Messenger of all said, Wash him with water and lote leaves, and shroud him in his two garments, and do not put any perfume on him or cover his head, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the Talbiyah",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2853-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2853-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2853-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6c4",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2854,
      "bookHadithIndex": 237,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn Abbas:That a man in Ihram was thrown by his she-camel and his neck was broken. It was said that he had died, so the Prophet said: \"Wash him with water and lotus leaves, and shroud him in two cloths.\" Then he said: \"Do not put any perfume on him for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the Talbiyah.\" Shubah said: \"Ten years later, I asked him (the narrator Abu Bishr) anbut that, and he narrated the Hadith as he had the first time, except that he said: 'And do not cover his face and head",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2854-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2854-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2854-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6c5",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2855,
      "bookHadithIndex": 238,
      "text": "It was narrated that Ibn Abbas said:\"While a man was standing in Arafat with the Messenger of Allah, he fell from his mount and it killed him. The Messenger of Allah said: 'Wash him with water and lotus leaves, and shroud him in two cloths. Do not apply aromatics to him or cover his head, for Allah, the Might and Sublime, wil raise him on the Day of Resurrection reciting the Talbiyah",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2855-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2855-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2855-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6c6",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2856,
      "bookHadithIndex": 239,
      "text": "It was narrated that Ibn Abbas said:\"The she-Camel of a ma in Ihram broke his neck and killed him. He was brought to the Messenger of Allah and he said 'Wash him and shroud him, and do not cover his head, or bring any perfume near him, for he will be raisd reciting Talbiyah.'\" (Sahih) Dies",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2856-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2856-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2856-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6c7",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2857,
      "bookHadithIndex": 240,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn Abbas that:a man was performing Hajj with the Messenger of Allah and his she-camel threw him and he died. The Messenger of Allah said: \"Wash him and shroud him in two garments, and do not cover his head of his face, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting Talbiyah",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2857-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2857-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2857-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6c8",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2858,
      "bookHadithIndex": 241,
      "text": "It was narrated that Ibn Abbas said:\"A man in Ihram came with the Messenger of Allah and fell from atop his camel, breaking his neck, and he died. The Messenger of Allah said: 'Wash him with water and lotus leaves, and wrap him in his two garments. But do not cover his head, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the Talbiyah",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2858-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2858-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2858-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6c9",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2859,
      "bookHadithIndex": 242,
      "text": "It was narrated from Nafi that:Abdulla bin Abdullah and salim bin Abdullah bin Umar when the army besiged Ibn Az-Zubair before he was killed. They said: \"It does not matter if you do not perform Hajj this year; we are afraid lest we are prevented from reaching the House.\" He Sadi: we went out with the Messenger of Allah and the disbelievers of the Quraish prevented us from reaching the House. So the Messenger of Allah slaughtered his Hadi and shave his head. I ask you to bear witness that I have resolved to peform Umrah. If Allah wills I will set out and if I am allowed to reach the House I will circumambulate it, and if I am prevented from reaching the House I will do what the Messenger of Allah did when I was with him.\" Then he traveled for a while, then he said: \"They are both the same. I ask you to bear witness that I have resolved to perform Hajj as well as Umrah. And he did not exit Ihram for either until he exited Ihram on the Day of Sacrifice and offered his Hadi",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2859-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2859-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2859-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6ca",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2860,
      "bookHadithIndex": 243,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ikrimah, from Al-Hajjaj bin Amr Al-Ansari that:he heard the Messenger of Allah say \"Whoever suffers a leg injury of breaks his leg, he has exited Ihram, but he has to perform another Hajj.\" I asked Ibn Abbas and Abu Hurarirah about that and he said \"He spoke the truth",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2860-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2860-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2860-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6cb",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2861,
      "bookHadithIndex": 244,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ikramah, from Al-Hajja bin Amr that the Prophet said:\"Whoever breaks his leg or suffers a leg injury, then he has exited Ihram, but he has to perform another Hajj.\" I asked Ibn 'Abbas and Abu Hurairah and the said: \"He spoke the thurth.\" And in his narration (one of the narrators) shuaib said: \"He has to perfom Hajj the following year",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2861-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2861-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2861-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6cc",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2862,
      "bookHadithIndex": 245,
      "text": "Ibn Umar narrated that:the Messenger of Allah used to dismount at Dhu Tuwa and stay there overnight unitl he prayed Subh when he was approaching Makkah. The place where the Messenger of Allah prayed was on top of the big hillock and not in the Masjid that was built later on, but it was lower than that, on top of the big hillock",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2862-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2862-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2862-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6cd",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2863,
      "bookHadithIndex": 246,
      "text": "It was narrated from Muhaarish Al-Kabi, that:the Prophet went out a night from Al-Jirranah when he set out for Umrah, and came back to Al-Jirranah when he set out for Umrah, and came back to Al-Jirranah in the morning, as if he had stayed there. Then, when the sun had passed its zenith he went out from Al-Jirranah in the valley of Sarif until the road joined the road to Al-Madinah from Sarif",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2863-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2863-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2863-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6ce",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2864,
      "bookHadithIndex": 247,
      "text": "It was narrated from Muharrish Al-Kabi that:the Prophet set out from Al-Jirranah at night as if he were an ingot of silver (i.e., in whiteness and purity) and perfomed Umrah, then he came back in the mooring as if he had stayed there overnight",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2864-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2864-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2864-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6cf",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2865,
      "bookHadithIndex": 248,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn Umar that:the Messenger of Allah entered Makkah from the upper valley which is in Al-Batha and he left from the lower valley",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2865-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2865-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2865-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6d0",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2866,
      "bookHadithIndex": 249,
      "text": "It was narrated from Jabir that:the Prophet enter Makkah and his standard was white",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2866-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2866-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2866-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c677dd1a4c9c86f0a6d1",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321",
      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2867,
      "bookHadithIndex": 250,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ansas that the Prophet entered Makkah wearing a helmet. It was said that Ibn Katal was haging on to the drapes of the Kabah and he said:\"Kill him",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2867-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2867-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2867-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}